<figure class="gallery__item"><a href="https://rudytrnka.com/media/posts/54/gallery/Qwen_Edit_2511_01615_.png" data-size="968x1296"><img loading="lazy" src="https://rudytrnka.com/media/posts/54/gallery/Qwen_Edit_2511_01615_-thumbnail.png" alt="" width="768" height="1028"></a></figure>
<figure class="gallery__item"><a href="https://rudytrnka.com/media/posts/54/gallery/Qwen_Edit_2511_01617_.png" data-size="968x1296"><img loading="lazy" src="https://rudytrnka.com/media/posts/54/gallery/Qwen_Edit_2511_01617_-thumbnail.png" alt="" width="768" height="1028"></a></figure>
<figure class="gallery__item"><a href="https://rudytrnka.com/media/posts/54/gallery/Qwen_Edit_2511_01595_.png" data-size="968x1296"><img loading="lazy" src="https://rudytrnka.com/media/posts/54/gallery/Qwen_Edit_2511_01595_-thumbnail.png" alt="" width="768" height="1028"></a></figure>
</div></div>
<p>This is a sketch that was unplanned, a surprise, and my first time drawing somebody posing just for me. I drove some Navy buddies home a few states away and one of them knew I liked to draw and he had a surprise for me. He leads me up stairs to a apartment and tells me this girl is for you to draw, well this was a surprise, I was not expecting this and honestly one of the coolest surprises anyone has given me. She was sitting in the room just as I drew her, she did ask me what I wanted her to do and I said as you are is fine. I will admit I could have done better but I just drove for 6 hours and was a little tired but was passing up the experience. This was fun to try different AI styles converting the image to a finished art piece.</p>
            ]]>
        </content>
    </entry>
